From: Andre Przywara <andre.przywara@arm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: backport A523 CPU cluster-B CCU for Cubie A5E bench

Narrow upstream v3 CPU clock model to cluster B and the explicit bench boot
option. Do not write any CPU PLL or mux on probe. Use the documented
temporary 600 MHz source and require factor commit, lock and mux readback.
The Radxa BSP confirms direct N encoding and cluster mux P postdivider.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/linux-sunxi/20260925225112.14081-4-andre.przywara@arm.com/
Link: https://github.com/radxa/allwinner-bsp/blob/cubie-aiot-v1.4.6/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun55iw3-displl.c#L81-L96
---
